sva.tooltip.plate.summary=§7Part of a Vehicle Charging Station's platform
sva.tooltip.plate.1=§eHelipad: "H" marking for helicopters and tiltrotors
sva.tooltip.plate.2=§eA landing light at the platform's edge - glows at night (light 7)
sva.tooltip.plate.details=Plates laid next to each other and to the station, on its level, make a platform of any shape (up to %s plates). The station charges vehicles standing on its plates. The platform's size decides what fits: 3x3 - hoverbike and buggy, 3x5 - crawler and drill, 5x5 - helicopter, plane and tiltrotor, 7x7 - jet, shuttle and Singular ship. Every plate over the vehicle's minimum adds +10%% charging speed (up to +200%%).
sva.tooltip.howto.plate=Lay the plates level with the station, starting next to it. Blue marking - charging, green - full. Made on the Engineering Workbench.
sva.tooltip.module.gas=§7Refuels gases right on the platform
sva.tooltip.module.gas.details=A Gas Column placed against the station or a plate joins the platform: the vehicle on it gets every gas it has a tank for (25 mB/t each) while it charges. The column itself then leaves that vehicle alone, so the rate is never doubled; the module also reaches far plates outside the column's radius. The column's rule applies: only its owner's vehicles.
sva.tooltip.module.repair=§7Mends hulls on the platform
sva.tooltip.module.repair.details=Repairs the hull of the vehicle on the platform: +1%% every 3 s, one Silicon Age steel ingot per 10%%. Ingots come from a chest (any inventory) against the station or a plate. Works only with wear on in the config.
sva.tooltip.module.access=§7The station owner's vehicles and his friends'
sva.tooltip.module.access.details=The station serves the vehicles of whoever placed it, and vehicles driven by a player with rights on one of the station owner's vehicles: he is on its access list or carries its key card. A vehicle with nobody at the wheel is served only if it is the station owner's. Without the module every vehicle on the platform charges.
sva.tooltip.howto.module=Put it in one of the three module slots of the station screen (right-click the station). Made on the Engineering Workbench ("Modules" tab).
